;; sarutahiko-factory-r0 — 建築手順 (construction procedure / 4D施工シーケンス),
;; Datomic-style EDN. SSoT for the ORDER in which the truck plant is built — full
;; MEP + 外構 + 出荷ヤード, each step assigned a 施工ロボット (:step/robot → robots.edn).
;; Same shape + toolchain as giemon-factory-r0/construction.edn (ADR-2606010030).
;;
;; The plant is designed to be BUILT by the tatekata 建方 robot fleet (ADR-2605250715).
;; `kotoba_gen.py` emits one kotoba entity per step (kg/claim/step/* datoms, EAVT),
;; with :step/depends-on / :step/consumes as ENTITY-REF claims + :step/robot, and a
;; flat construction.order.json consumed by kami-app-sarutahiko-factory's 4D viewer.
;;
;; :step/robot       施工ロボット id (robots.edn :robot/registry)
;; :step/depends-on  vector of prior :step/id (predecessors → entity refs)
;; :step/consumes    vector of :part/id from building.edn (materials drawn)
;; :step/reveals     vector of render element ids in factory.scene.json
;; :step/duration-d  nominal duration in working days (schedule)
;; :step/trade       responsible trade / 工種

{:proc/meta
 {:proc/of        "sarutahiko-factory-r0"
  :proc/revision  "v1"
  :proc/title     "猿田彦 truck plant — R0 construction sequence (4D, full MEP + 外構 + 出荷ヤード + 施工ロボット)"
  :proc/method    "robotic design-build, single 180x90m bay, heavy steel portal frame + 構内外構 + 出荷ヤード"
  :proc/note      "R0 design sequence. depends-on encodes hard logic; :step/robot assigns the construction robot per trade (robots.edn). Durations are nominal; the buildability check estimates robot cycle-time vs these. Heavy steel uses robot:crane (24m reach) for the 90m clear-span trusses."}

